"Which notation is often used for the identity function on $X$?","options":["$\\Gamma_X$","$\\operatorname{id}_X$","$f^{-1}_X$","$\\int_X$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"ba44bdd433e851b40e0968de","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_identity_function_3718b706_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"If $x\\in X$, what is $\\operatorname{id}_X(x)$?","options":["$0$","$x$","$1$","$-x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"959eb46f4a3943143a3c6292","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_identity_function_3718b706_004","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"On $X = \\{2,5\\}$, what is $\\operatorname{id}_X(5)$?","options":["$2$","$7$","$5$","$0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"061873462fa3f91f483c6bd8","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_identity_function_3718b706_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What happens when any function is composed with the identity function in the appropriate domain and codomain?","options":["It becomes the zero function.","It is left unchanged.","It becomes non-bijective.","It becomes undefined everywhere."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3adcb5d4bc908404c25bf058","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_identity_function_3718b706_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which property of the identity function is correct?","options":["It is never bijective.","It is bijective and is its own inverse.","It has no inverse.","It changes every element of $X$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"9a8d17d7ffe972b4f07bf9a1","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_identity_function_3718b706_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $g\\colon X\\to Y$. Which composition equals $g$?","options":["$\\operatorname{id}_X\\circ g$","$g\\circ\\operatorname{id}_X$","$g\\circ g$","$\\operatorname{id}_X\