72e976","time_limit":40},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_identity_function_3718b706_012","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ be a bijection. Which identity relation is stated for $f\\circ f^{-1}$?","options":["$f\\circ f^{-1} = \\operatorname{id}_Y$","$f\\circ f^{-1} = \\operatorname{id}_X$","$f\\circ f^{-1} = f$","$f\\circ f^{-1} = f^{-1}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"8774194696316d15a97a840b","time_limit":40},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"What is the graph of the identity function $\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbb{R}}$?","options":["the line $y=x$","the $x$-axis","a horizontal line","a parabola"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"88a4d829a550e7c0e76f0b96","time_limit":20},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Is $\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbb{R}}(x)=x$ strictly increasing?","options":["Yes","No, it is constant","No, it is decreasing","Only on $[0,\\infty)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"89dbd3f7fa5fadf50f76e5a5","time_limit":30},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Which property of the identity function is stated?","options":["It is never injective.","It is bijective and its own inverse.","It has no inverse.","It changes every input to a fixed value."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b89f365d0eb0bd562e39c0ee","time_limit":20},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"What is the derivative of $\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbb{R}}(x)=x$?","options":["$1$","$0$","$x$","undefined"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"233bd19082f8e6331987e28e","time_limit":30},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_005","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is $\\operatorname{id}_{\\mathbb{R}}(-3)$?","options":["$-3$","$0$","$3$","$9$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d2310fd0d53c602c0e68d76f","time_limit":20},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_006","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $f\\colon\\mathbb{R}\\to\\mathbb{R}$ be any function and $\\operatorname{id}(x)=x$. Which identity holds for every real $x$?","options":["$(f\\circ\\operatorname{id})(x)=f(x)$","$(f\\circ\\operatorname{id})(x)=x$","$(f\\circ\\operatorname{id})(x)=0$","$(f\\circ\\operatorname{id})(x)=f(f(x))$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dfa774e8524de29635be5743","time_limit":30},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_007","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Why does the subscript in $\\operatorname{id}_X$ matter?","options":["It specifies the set whose elements are left unchanged.","It specifies the derivative order.","It specifies an exponent.","It specifies an integration bound for the variable being kept fixed."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c667406d05e55409b97ff32e","time_limit":30},{"id":"identity_function_expansion_008","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f\\colon X\\to Y$ be a bijection and let $y\\in Y$. What is $(f\\circ f^{-1})(y)$?","options":["$f(y)$","$f^{-1}(y)$","$0$","$y$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"70ddc3a83730ddaf1272b2fb","time_limit":30}]}}